@ifnottex
@node Top
@top Lena — An Emacs major mode for Lean

Lena is a set of packages that extend @uref{https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/, GNU Emacs} for the @uref{https://lean-lang.org, Lean} language. It is
ISTA PLV's fork of @uref{https://codeberg.org/mekeor/nael, Nael} by Mekeor Melire, which is itself a radically refactored
fork of @uref{https://github.com/leanprover-community/lean4-mode, Lean4-Mode} with focus on simplicity, modularity and integration into
Emacs' core. Lena branched from Nael 0.8.3 and adds an infoview, signs in the
margin and more. See @emph{Lineage and Credits} for more information about Lena's
lineage.

The @code{lena} package defines the major mode. It also introduces simple and two-sided
abbreviations per @uref{https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Abbrevs.html, Abbrev} and @uref{https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/autotype/, Skeleton} respectively. It teaches Emacs' built-in
@uref{https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/, LSP} client @uref{https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/eglot/, Eglot} about @uref{https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/master/src/Lean/Data/Lsp/Extra.lean, Lean-specific LSP-extensions}, tells @uref{https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Programming-Language-Doc.html, ElDoc} to display that
information, and shows it in an infoview, like the “@uref{https://github.com/leanprover/vscode-lean4/blob/master/vscode-lean4/manual/manual.md#infoview, info view}” in @uref{https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=leanprover.lean4, vscode-lean}
that many are familiar with. The separate package @code{lena-evil} binds keys for @uref{https://github.com/emacs-evil/evil, Evil}.

Lena works with Eglot only. Nael's support for @uref{https://github.com/emacs-lsp/lsp-mode, lsp-mode}, its package @code{nael-lsp},
is not part of Lena.

Much of the code that Lena adds to Nael was written with the help of an AI
assistant, Claude, and reviewed, tested and revised by Lena's maintainers, who
answer for it. The code that Lena takes from Nael and the other projects named
under @emph{Lineage and Credits} is their authors' work. 

@end ifnottex

