@node Lineage
@section Lineage

@itemize
@item
@uref{https://github.com/leanprover-community/lean4-mode, Lean4-Mode} is the Lean community's Emacs mode for Lean 4.
@item
Nael is Mekeor Melire's fork of it, on @uref{https://codeberg.org/mekeor/nael, Codeberg} and @uref{https://melpa.org/#/nael, Melpa}. Lena's major mode,
its Font-Lock rules, abbreviations, navigation and much of this manual are
Nael's.
@item
Lena branched from Nael 0.8.3 (commit @samp{c1d3497} of Nael's @samp{release} branch) and
was later renamed to Lena.
@item
It builds on code from elsewhere: @code{lena-eglot.el}'s building of imports
(@samp{dependencyBuildMode}) and restarting of files are adapted from Doug Torrance's
@uref{https://github.com/d-torrance/lean4-mode, lean4-mode}; @code{lena-rpc.el} is derived from that lean4-mode's @samp{lean4-rpc.el}, which
is derived from Jan Mas Rovira's @uref{https://github.com/janmasrovira/neo-lean-mode, neo-lean-mode}; the Doom Emacs module follows
Doom Emacs' own @samp{:lang lean} module. See @emph{License and Maintenance} and @samp{NOTICE}.
@end itemize

